      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- department: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- department name: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- term code: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- 2019FA: ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE\n- Mathematics: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subjects: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- total number of subjects: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- total units: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- average total units: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- average number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- highest average number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.COURSE_NUMBER <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects in the academic term with the term code '2019FA' that are in the Mathematics department, show the subject ID, subject title, department name, total units, and the rank of each subject within its department (ordered by subject ID).\n```sql\nSELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.TOTAL_UNITS, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS t0 JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2019FA' AND t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\n```\n2. For each department, give the department name and calculate the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students, departments whose name is not null, and only include departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment, MAX(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_range, VARIANCE(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrollment_variance FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED l ON s.COURSE_NUMBER = l.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY s.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY enrollment_range DESC;\n```\n3. For each department in the academic term with the term code '2019FA', list the department name, the total number of subjects in that department, and the average total units for its subjects. For each department, also include a grand total for all departments in the format of (null, total subjects, average total units).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t1.SUBJECT_ID, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.TOTAL_UNITS, RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS window_column FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS t0 JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2019FA' AND t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' ), DepartmentStats AS ( SELECT t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(DISTINCT t1.SUBJECT_ID) AS total_subjects, AVG(t1.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units FROM ACADEMIC_TERMS t0 JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY t1 ON t0.TERM_CODE = t1.TERM_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2019FA' GROUP BY t1.DEPARTMENT_NAME ) SELECT ds.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ds.total_subjects, ds.avg_total_units FROM DepartmentStats ds UNION ALL SELECT NULL AS DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUM(ds.total_subjects) AS total_subjects, AVG(ds.avg_total_units) AS avg_total_units FROM DepartmentStats ds ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME\n```\n4. For each department, give the department name and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students, departments whose name is not null, and only include departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, l.TERM_CODE, AVG(l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment_per_term FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE s JOIN LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED l ON s.COURSE_NUMBER = l.COURSE_NUMBER WHERE l.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL AND s.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, l.TERM_CODE ) SELECT DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(avg_enrollment_per_term) AS highest_avg_enrollment_per_term FROM inner_cte GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each department in the academic term with the term code '2019FA', list the department name, the total number of subjects in that department, the average total units for its subjects, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department (considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students, departments whose name is not null, and only including departments whose name is 'Mathematics' (Course 18)). For each department, also include a grand total for all departments in the format of (null, total subjects, average total units, null). Do not return any rounded answers."
