ics tied to actual enrollment records or subject groups per term → use SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\"\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures** — NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (headcount snapshots incl. LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) vs SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (registrar official); decision guide: \"enrollment of subjects within the … library reserve scope → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS.\"\n- **column_concept_department_name** — DEPARTMENT_NAME (catalog/summary/lookup tables) vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME (offering/program tables); same academic value domain.\n- **column_concept_term_code** — universal YYYYTT join key across term dimension and fact tables.\n\n**Metric precedents:** dw_1766 (contains the exact \"highest average number of enrolled students in any term\" CTE), dw_2597, dw_4387, dw_3911 (grand-total-row pattern), dw_1301, dw_4584, dw_4658, dw_4724, dw_4683, dw_4812, dw_3311, dw_1288, dw_2180, dw_1221, dw_1165, dw_2591, dw_3436, dw_4458, dw_4566, dw_4583, dw_4701, dw_4826, dw_4978, dw_2628, dw_3248, dw_3357, dw_3393, dw_3736, dw_3959, dw_4069 (metrics on LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY joins → ACADEMIC_TERMS / ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL (TERM_CODE); joined from TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED; joins → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION. Member of concept_subject_offering_facts; carries column_concepts term_code, subject_id, department_name, enrollment_measures, total_units, master_subject_id.\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED joins → ACADEMIC_TERMS, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, TIP_DETAIL, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL; joined from SIS_SUBJECT_CODE (COURSE_NUMBER), LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL. Member of concept_subject_offering_facts and concept_course_material_programs. 28 metrics depend on it.\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE joins → SIS_DEPARTMENT, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED; joined from COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.\n- dw_1766 lineage: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ⋈ LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (COURSE_NUMBER) for the enrollment CTE — identical to the required fourth column.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (enrollment measure candidates):**\n| Candidate | Granularity | Coverage | Measure | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | subject per term, library-reserve scope | library reserve processing only | headcount snapshot | table desc; column_concept_enrollment_measures |\n| SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER | subject per term, registrar | all registrar subjects | official final enrollment | column_concept_enrollment_measures decision guide |\n| SUBJECT_OFFERED(_SUMMARY).NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | section / subject per term | registrar offerings | headcount | column_concept_enrollment_measures |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- \"total number of subjects\" & \"average total units\" per department in term '2019FA' → SUBJECT_SUMMARY (SUBJECT_ID, TOTAL_UNITS, DEPARTMENT_NAME, TERM_CODE): SUPPORTED (hint mapping + decision guide \"unit statistics tied to enrollment records per term → SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\"). COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: NOT-SUPPORTED per hint mapping.\n- \"highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department … more than 0 enrolled students … 'Mathematics' (Course 18)\" → SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME + LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS joined on COURSE_NUMBER: SUPPORTED (hint join keys; dw_1766 precedent uses exactly this).\n- Term filter '2019FA' → ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE = SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE: SUPPORTED.\n- Grand total row (null, total subjects, average total units, null): SUPPORTED via UNION ALL over department stats (dw_3911/hint subquery 3 pattern).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"department name\" maps