mpossible this session. Noted explicitly.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n**6a.** Use ACADEMIC_TERMS ⋈ SUBJECT_SUMMARY (TERM_CODE) filtered to '2019FA' for department name / COUNT(DISTINCT SUBJECT_ID) / AVG(TOTAL_UNITS); use SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ⋈ LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED (COURSE_NUMBER) with NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0, DEPARTMENT_NAME IS NOT NULL, DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics', two-level aggregation (AVG per term, then MAX across terms) for the fourth column; LEFT JOIN the enrollment CTE onto department stats; UNION ALL a grand-total row (NULL, SUM(total_subjects), AVG(avg_total_units), NULL); ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME.\n\n**6b/6c.** Data: SUBJECT_SUMMARY is one row per subject per term (no fan-out with the single-row-per-term ACADEMIC_TERMS filter); the enrollment CTE is aggregated to one row per department before the LEFT JOIN, so no fan-out. Semantic-network: hint join keys and column mappings match exactly; column_concept decision guides route TOTAL_UNITS to SUBJECT_SUMMARY and library-scope enrollment to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS. Business: dw_1766 is a verbatim precedent for the enrollment CTE; hint subquery 3 is a verbatim precedent for the department stats + grand-total UNION ALL shape.\n\n**6d.** No balanced alternatives — the hint mapping and dw_1766 precedent uniquely determine the tables. Caveat: could not execute due to persistent DB access denial; SQL follows verified precedents syntactically (MySQL 8 nested CTE as in dw_1766).\n\n",
